{
  "tema": 7274,
  "slug": "gustar-de",
  "titulo": "Gustar de + noun / infinitive (formal, literary)",
  "subtitulo": "La señora gustaba de leer poesía.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "In formal or literary Spanish, gustar de + noun or infinitive works like a normal verb: the person is the subject: Antonio gusta de la buena comida. Compare everyday a Antonio le gusta la buena comida. Also: ¿Gusta? (polite offer, very Mexican).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "subject + gustar (conjugated for the person)",
            "+ de +",
            "noun / infinitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Formal and literary: the **person is the subject**, unlike everyday **me gusta**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With nouns, the article is optional: **gusta de (la) buena comida**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Related polite Mexican use: **¿Gusta?** (_Would you like some?_), offering food; **¿Gusta pasar?** (_Would you like to come in?_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **gustar de** sounds like a 19th-century novel; **¿gusta?** sounds like a Mexican grandma."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "La señora de la casa ==gustaba de== tratar bien a sus empleadas.",
              "en": "The lady of the house liked to treat her staff well."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los vecinos ==gustaban de== reunirse en las noches a platicar.",
              "en": "The neighbors liked to get together in the evenings to chat."
            },
            {
              "es": "Antonio ==gusta de== la buena comida y frecuenta restaurantes excelentes.",
              "en": "Antonio enjoys good food and frequents excellent restaurants."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi profesor ==gusta de== las obras clásicas.",
              "en": "My professor is fond of the classics."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Gusta==? Están recién hechos.",
              "en": "Would you like some? They're freshly made."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
